	(text_box "Differences\n\nEK uses PC11/SPI0_NPCS1\nWe use: PA3/SPI0_NPCS0\n\n\nConfusion in the EK:\nDataflash on SPI0 uses:\nPA0, PA1, PA2, PC11\n- PA2 CLK is connected with PA8 CLK of MMCB SDcard\n- PA8 is MMCK for both MCIA and MCIB (both SD slots)\n- Why is PA2 / SPI0 clk shared with MCI clk PA8 with a resistor???\n\n\nBoot prog:\nMCI1 SDcard:\nPA6 PA7 PA8 PA9 PA10 PA11\n\nDataflash on SPI0:\nPA0 PA1 PA2 PA3\nPA3: CS0\nPC11: CS1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 20.32 0)
		(size 76.2 50.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2c2df470-ea42-4622-be54-546bd33730b5")
	)
	(text_box "NAND pins\n\nNANDOE and NANDWE are dedicated\nCE is either NCS3/NANDCS (PC) or any available gpio\nRDY is any available GPIO\n\nTODO: confirm WP polarity and if we're using 8bit or 16bit\nDo we need to do RDY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.04 20.32 0)
		(size 86.36 58.42)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
